course: dictionary
lesson: 12431
title: Deceitful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deceitful describes someone who tricks people or tells lies to make them believe something that is not true. A deceitful person hides the truth on purpose. «The fox smiled and promised the hens he was their friend, but he was planning to trap them.» The clues are smiled and promised, but then planning to trap them. The friendly words hide a trick, so deceitful means tricking people.
explain: Deceitful can describe a person, an action, a word or a smile. «She gave him a deceitful smile» means her smile was meant to fool him. Look for clue words like lied, tricked, hid and pretended. They often show that someone is being deceitful.
explain: Deceitful is in the same family as deceive, which means to fool someone. Honest is the opposite. An honest person tells the truth, even when it is hard.
fact: Deceitful means tricking people with lies or hidden plans.
fact: «Deceitful» can describe a person, an action or a word.
fact: «A deceitful smile» is a smile meant to hide the truth or to fool someone.
fact: In stories, deceitful characters, like the wolf in «Little Red Riding Hood», use lies to get what they want, so readers learn not to trust them.
fact: Deceitful messages online, such as a fake prize message asking for your password, are scams. Never share private information because of a message like that.
exercise: «The seller was deceitful. He said the old watch was solid gold, but it was only painted metal.» What does deceitful mean here? | *Tricking people with lies | Kind to animals | Very tired | Honest and open
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as deceitful? | Generous | *Dishonest | Cheerful | Honest
exercise: «A deceitful message said you had won a prize, so click here and type your password.» What is the message trying to do? | Say thank you for your help | Give you a real prize | *Trick you into giving away private information | Teach you to type faster
test: «The cat hid the fish bones and told everyone it was not him. It was a deceitful trick.» What does deceitful show about the cat? | Being very hungry | Feeling sleepy after a big meal | *Hiding the truth to avoid blame | Enjoying a game of football
test: Which is a deceitful action? | Sharing your sweets fairly | *Pretending to be asleep so you do not have to help clean up | Saying sorry when you have hurt a friend | Telling the truth about breaking the vase, even though you will get told off
exam: «The deceitful fox smiled and promised the hens he was their friend.» Which word shows the fox is tricking them? | Promised | Smiled | Friend | *Deceitful
